                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>Milab DC-63 is a multipattern condenser mic with Milab&#8217;s characteristic rectangular capsule.</p><p>The mic&#8217;s polar pattern and other settings are selected by a combination of two ring switches and a potentiometer on the microphone body. This provides 44 combinations of pattern, 12dB pad and high pass filtering.</p><p>The DC-63 uses a rectangular dual membrane condenser capsule and dual FET preamplifier. The capsule is shockmounted with silicon rubber to reduce mechanical noise.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Milab/DC-63">Milab Microphones DC-63</a> is also known as: DC63.</p><p>The mic was released in 1982.</p>
